edit(a,0,summary='Use operating cash flow and capital spending alongside net income to assess an ecommerce store\'s available cash.',steps=['Reconcile net income to operating cash flow using non-cash expenses and working-capital movements.','A common free cash flow definition is operating cash flow minus positive cash capital expenditure; state the definition used.','Do not subtract a negative investing cash flow number or assume every investing transaction is capital expenditure.','Depreciation and amortisation affect profit but are non-cash expenses in that period.','Add financing flows separately to explain the change in bank cash; borrowing can raise cash without improving free cash flow.'])
edit(a,2,steps=['Compare units-sold COGS with inventory purchased and supplier payment dates.','Track deposits, balances due, inventory receipts and payables to explain cash timing.','An inventory balance increase is not automatically an equal cash payment; supplier credit and prepayments change the bridge.','Forecast cash at planned reorder dates and stress-test slower sell-through.'])
edit(a,4,steps=['Separate software costs expensed immediately from costs qualifying for capitalization under the applicable policy.','Record actual cash paid even where the P&L recognizes amortisation over later periods.','Reconcile asset additions, amortisation, payables and non-cash changes; the asset balance change alone is not cash spending.','Subtract relevant capitalized development cash expenditure in the stated free cash flow definition.','Treat the source\'s amortisation period as an example, not a rule for every ecommerce platform.'])
edit(a,5,title='Schedule cash tax payments using the store\'s actual tax calendar',summary='Profit-based monthly tax estimates can differ from actual payment dates; reserve cash for the confirmed schedule.',steps=['Obtain the entity\'s actual tax payment calendar and amounts from the accountant.','Forecast payments in the periods cash is due, whether monthly, quarterly or another schedule.','Reconcile tax expense, tax payable and payments.','Keep cash reserved for upcoming obligations out of discretionary spending decisions.'])
